; ============================================================================
; Native package calls from the JS backend: a local WebAssembly module.
;
; `bind = wasm` + `wasm = './math-wasm.mjs'` imports the wasm module through an
; ESM wrapper (math-wasm.mjs, next to this file) and forwards each #{c} extern
; to the wasm export of the same C symbol name (`square` -> `square`). A
; relative specifier is a plain local file: no npm install, no dependencies
; entry, no CDN import-map entry.
;
; Run it (Node, no npm install needed):
;   no run --js main.no          -> prints 42.25 then 42
;
; The wasm binary is generated by gen-math-wasm.mjs (node script, no
; toolchain); math-wasm.mjs also documents how a browser-targeted module
; resolves its ready Promise before native calls.
; ============================================================================

#{bind=wasm, wasm='./math-wasm.mjs'}
# /math

; WebAssembly export `square` (imported through the ESM wrapper): squares its argument
; x f64: value to square
; r f64: x * x

#{c}
square = (x f64) (r f64)

; WebAssembly export `answer`: returns the constant 42, no arguments
; r i32: always 42

#{c}
answer = () (r i32)

; 入口由編譯器合成，直接寫頂層陳述（'main' 是保留名，不能再當函式名）
print(square(6.5))
print(answer())
